There's no existing project in the working directory. Let me show you the implementation pattern you need. You'll add two things:

### 1. Create `Middleware/ApiExceptionHandler.cs`

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace YourApp.Middleware;

internal sealed class ApiExceptionHandler(ILogger<ApiExceptionHandler> logger)
    : IExceptionHandler
{
    public async ValueTask<bool> TryHandleAsync(
        HttpContext httpContext,
        Exception exception,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var (statusCode, title) = exception switch
        {
            KeyNotFoundException => (StatusCodes.Status404NotFound, "Not Found"),
            ArgumentException   => (StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest, "Bad Request"),
            InvalidOperationException => (StatusCodes.Status409Conflict, "Conflict"),
            _ => (0, (string?)null)
        };

        if (statusCode == 0)
            return false; // Fall through to default handler (returns 500, no details)

        logger.LogWarning(exception, "Handled API exception: {Title}", title);

        httpContext.Response.StatusCode = statusCode;
        await httpContext.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(new ProblemDetails
        {
            Status = statusCode,
            Title = title,
            Detail = title,        // Never use exception.Message — it may leak internals
            Instance = httpContext.Request.Path
        }, cancellationToken);

        return true;
    }
}
```

### 2. Register in `Program.cs`

Add these lines **before** `var app = builder.Build()`:

```csharp
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<ApiExceptionHandler>();
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();
```

Add these lines **after** `var app = builder.Build()` but **before** any `app.Map*` calls:

```csharp
app.UseExceptionHandler();   // Catches exceptions, routes to IExceptionHandler
app.UseStatusCodePages();    // Converts bare status codes to Problem Details
```

### How it works

- **Known exceptions** (`KeyNotFoundException`, `ArgumentException`, `InvalidOperationException`) are caught by your `ApiExceptionHandler` and mapped to the correct status code with a safe Problem Details body.
- **Unhandled exceptions** return `false` from `TryHandleAsync`, so the default `UseExceptionHandler` middleware returns a `500` Problem Details response with no sensitive details (enabled by `AddProblemDetails()`).
- No `try-catch` needed in any endpoint — the middleware handles everything globally.

### Example response

```json
{
  "type": "https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc9110#section-15.5.5",
  "title": "Not Found",
  "status": 404,
  "detail": "Not Found",
  "instance": "/api/products/999"
}
```
